<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia</h1><p class="st-meta">1815 CE – 1866 CE · capital Milan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Austrian-ruled kingdom of Lombardy and Venetia, centre of Habsburg power in Italy and target of the wars of Italian independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1815 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> and the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a>, which joined them as a kingdom with the emperor as king, governed by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, at first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-rainer-joseph-of-austria">Archduke Rainer</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Lombardy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> had an efficient administration, good schools and a prosperous economy, but censorship and police repression made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> unpopular; the patriot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silvio-pellico">Silvio Pellico</a> described his imprisonment in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spilberk-castle">Spielberg</a> fortress. In 1848 the Five Days of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-san-marco">Republic of San Marco</a> drove out the Austrians, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-radetzky-von-radetz">Marshal Radetzky</a> reconquered both. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-of-mexico">Archduke Maximilian</a> tried liberal reforms as governor-general in 1857–1859.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-solferino">Solferino</a> in 1859 cost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>. After the war of 1866, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: FDRMRZUSA. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Lombardy%E2%80%93Venetia_(1815%E2%80%931866).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1815 CE – 1866 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Milan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Francis I of Austria, Archduke Rainer, Archduke Maximilian</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Lombard, Venetian, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lombardy-Venetia, Regno Lombardo-Veneto</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia" aria-label="Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4898 574 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5218 830L5218 830M5218 830L5381 747M5218 830L5226 1028M5218 830L5304 942M5218 830L5293 831M5218 830L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0M5381 747h0M5226 1028h0M5304 942h0M5293 831h0M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 830h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Milan. <a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
